findings.body:
`CleanupHandles` runs inside `finally`, before `ExitReadLock`/`ExitWriteLock`, and it can throw a `Win32Exception`. It can also throw `ObjectDisposedException` from SafeHandle marshaling, because `DangerousRelease` runs before `SetHandleInformation(safeHandle, ...)` and may drop the last ref.

If it throws:
- the remaining handles are never released or un-inherited;
- the original exception is masked;
- `s_processStartLock` is never exited, so every later `Process.Start` deadlocks.

Fix: clear the inherit flag before releasing, avoid throwing from cleanup, and exit the lock in its own `finally`.

